Z||000003||mwbackus||10-13-1999||04:39 PM||||I repainted both engine vent grills with high temperature gloss black engine paint. They do see a significant amount of heat, and, this is primarily responsible for degradation in appearance over time.  I also removed the grate things on the bottom of the grills (I never drive it in adverse wheather and it lives in a garage). I have found that they are much more functional (ie..enhanced cooling), and IMO, look much better than brand new grills.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000004||Eric||10-13-1999||06:51 PM||||I drill the rivets out of my engine cooling vents in order to paint the lower grate.  I know see these are going to be a real pain to reinstall, so I might just leave them off.  While they were off, my car was caught outside in some severe downpours and the thing started up and ran fine.<P>I painted my plastic interior parts with Plastikote paint.  It was black, but I'm sure they would make a clear also.  I painted all the light gray parts and so far there is no sign of cracking or pealing.  One thing about painting with that kind of paint, wait until the humidity is low because when the air is moist the glossy paint drys matte.||||reg||1
